{
 "id": "189-14",
 "split": "setup_long",
 "sentences": [
  "By involving representatives from various teams, we can ensure that the program is fair and that achievements are recognized regardless of the team or department.",
  "Going forward, I'd like to schedule regular meetings to discuss the progress and fine-tune the details.",
  "It's important that we keep our personal and work lives separate, especially when it comes to client communication.",
  "And remember, if you have any questions or concerns, don't hesitate to reach out.",
  "Remember, my door is always open if you need any guidance or support.",
  "Please do, and don't hesitate to reach out if you need anything at all.",
  "We're all looking forward to seeing what you accomplish here.",
  "Empowering our employees to work remotely also reduces overhead costs associated with physical offices.",
  "I'll make sure your thoughts are included as we shape and improve our employee benefits offerings.",
  "Work-life balance is crucial for long-term productivity and satisfaction.",
  "It's all about finding what works best for you and your team.",
  "Sometimes, it's as simple as shifting your work hours slightly to accommodate personal obligations or to take advantage of your most productive times of the day.",
  "Don't hesitate to discuss it with your team lead and find a schedule that suits you.",
  "So, if you ever need to work remotely, even if it's just for a day, don't hesitate to do so.",
  "From now on, I want you to end all function argument names with '_x'.",
  "Exactly.",
  "It's a small detail, but it helps keep the code clean and understandable for your colleagues and future contributors."
 ],
